# The recovery after a melee hit (#323) and the swing speed over the frame time (#352) in the test playground (#321):
# after a hit the weapon hand recovers for its weapon type's time (cfg.ini vr_melee_recovery_dagger / _1h / _2h, by default
# 0.6 / 0.8 / 1.0 s) - a swing started within it hits nothing, a swing after it hits. The same swings at 90 Hz and at
# 45 Hz give the same hits.
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -Playground -VrSim idle -Sequence melee-recovery
# The swings are ramps of the simulated right controller (0.85 m in 89 ms: 8 frames at 90 Hz, 4 at 45 Hz). The timeline
# counts frames, not seconds, and a busy runner plays far below the simulator's rate (41.8 fps on CI, #409: 33 frames
# lasted 0.8 s, past the dagger's 0.6 s), so the second swing of a pair goes straight back, two still frames after the
# first: it starts within the recovery at any rate down to ~14 fps. It may also fall within the per-target cooldown
# (0.25 s), so its own marker shows that the recovery refused it: `recovering`, `result=recovering` (such a swing never
# runs the strike check). The swing after the recovery waits for `recovery.left` to reach 0, a time.
# Swings are counted with ge, hits exactly: the simulated hand moves a step per frame, not per second, so a frame that
# stalls (a hit's effects) slows it for real and may split one ramp into two swings - the host test MeleeSwingTest
# proves the same swings at 45, 90 and an uneven 90 Hz.
@sim idle
@playground

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert area eq 30
# A level started with --loadlevel stays in the engine's cursor mode, which keeps the inventory open (no swings while it
# is); free look closes it, as loading a save does (a test-only workaround until #394)
freelook on
@until vr.melee.refused ne inventory 5s

# 1. The dagger's recovery: the default 0.6 s (the dagger shortest, 1h 0.8, 2h 1.0 - host test MeleeSwingTest). The
# game's own strike of every type is reported next to it, read from the hero's animations (one weapon is equipped: a
# script equip leaves the weapon it replaces on the cursor, an item dragged - no swings)
inventory playeraddfromscene dagger_9001
dagger_9001.equip player
@until vr.melee.recovery.weapon eq dagger 5s
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
@assert vr.melee.recovery.source eq default
@assert vr.melee.recovery.seconds eq 0.6
@assert vr.melee.recovery.games.dagger gt 0
@assert vr.melee.recovery.games.1h gt 0
@assert vr.melee.recovery.games.2h gt 0
@log melee\.recovery weapon=dagger seconds=0\.60 source=default game=\S+ dagger=\S+\.tea 1h=\S+\.tea 2h=\S+\.tea

# The peaceful goblin 60 units ahead, the dagger level with its chest, the hand to the right - moved there slowly
playground place 60
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
vr-sim head rot 0 -25 0
@frames 75
@assert playground.npcAlive eq true
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 0
@shot goblin-in-reach

# 2. At 90 Hz: a swing through the goblin and straight back - one hit; the second swing is in the recovery
@mark
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35; vr-sim @+11-18 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 2 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.recovery.recovering eq true
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 1
@assert vr.melee.recovery.swings ge 1
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=recovering .*hits=0
# A third swing once the recovery is over: it hits
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge {swings+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@frames 30
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 2
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit

# 3. At 45 Hz the same swings (half the frames, the same still pause between them): the same hits. A fresh goblin first (the respawn
# lever), so that the hits so far cannot have killed it
playground kill
@until playground.npcAlive eq false 5s
playground pull respawn
@until playground.npcAlive eq true 5s
playground place 60
vr-sim rate 45
@frames 20
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
@remember recovering vr.melee.recovery.swings
@mark
vr-sim @+1-4 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35; vr-sim @+7-10 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge {swings+2} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.recovery.recovering eq true
@frames 15
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 3
@assert vr.melee.recovery.swings ge {recovering+1}
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=recovering .*hits=0
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
vr-sim @+1-4 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge {swings+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@frames 15
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 4
@log melee\.swing kind=slash result=hit
@assert vr.melee.jumps eq 0
@assert errors eq 0
